# Verify before wrap-up

After making code or config changes in this repo, before ending the turn as "done", run the checks below that apply. Fix failures before concluding.

Skip only for pure Q&A / no file edits, or when the user explicitly says not to.

## Always

1. `pnpm check` (Biome) from the monorepo root.
2. `pnpm --filter @next-server-tools/standalone exec tsc -b` (or `pnpm build` if dist output is needed).

## When `packages/standalone/src/**` (or its tests) changed

3. `pnpm test` (unit suite).

## When boot / standalone / CLI / extensions / request path changed

4. `pnpm test:examples`, or at least the affected smoke case (e.g. `next-15 start`).

Typical triggers: `boot-server.ts`, `standalone-entry.ts`, `server.ts`, `replace-standalone.ts`, `start-standalone.ts`, `cli.ts`, `extension/**`, listen/TLS wiring.

## When docs or public API surface changed

5. Skim that `README.md`, `docs/TECHNICAL.md`, and `llms.txt` still match the code (exports, CLI, published `files`, bootstrap path).

## Do not do unless asked

- Git commit / push / PR
- Release or publish dry-runs
- Regenerating the lockfile (unless dependencies changed)
- Updating ROADMAP / review canvases unless ship readiness meaningfully changed
